Algorithm:

Start with two pointers p and q.
Set p to the first node of L1 and q to the first node of L2.
Compare the values of p and q.
Take the smaller value and add it to the new linked list.
Move the pointer of the list from which the smaller value was taken.
Repeat steps 3–5 until one of the lists becomes empty.
Add all the remaining nodes of the other list to the new linked list.
The new linked list is the merged sorted list.
